### Authentication API
# Execute as requisicoes na ordem: o cadastro e o login alimentam as variaveis usadas abaixo.
# Ao rodar via Aspire, ajuste @baseUrl para o endpoint exibido no dashboard.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080
@email = fulano@example.com
@password = Senha123

### Cadastrar usuario (publico)
# @name createUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Fulano de Tal",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "cpf": "529.982.247-25",
  "phone": "(11) 98765-4321",
  "birthDate": "1990-05-10",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Login (publico) - retorna o JWT
# Rate limiting: 5 tentativas por IP a cada 60s (padrao). Excedentes recebem 429 + Retry-After.
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

###
@userId = {{createUser.response.body.$.id}}
@token = {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Consultar usuario por Id
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Listar usuarios (paginado, com busca opcional por nome/e-mail)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users?page=1&pageSize=20&search=fulano
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Atualizar dados cadastrais (CPF e imutavel)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Fulano de Tal Silva",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "phone": "(11) 3333-4444",
  "birthDate": "1990-05-10"
}

### Trocar senha
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/password
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "{{password}}",
  "newPassword": "NovaSenha456"
}

### Criar permissao (recurso + acao; exposta como "users:read")
# @name createPermission
POST {{baseUrl}}/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "resource": "users",
  "action": "read",
  "description": "Consultar usuarios"
}

###
@permissionId = {{createPermission.response.body.$.id}}

### Consultar permissao por Id
GET {{baseUrl}}/permissions/{{permissionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Listar permissoes (paginado, filtros opcionais por recurso e acao - igualdade exata)
GET {{baseUrl}}/permissions?page=1&pageSize=20&resource=users&action=read
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Criar role (nome unico entre as ativas, sem diferenciar maiusculas/minusculas)
# @name createRole
POST {{baseUrl}}/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Suporte N2",
  "description": "Atendimento de segundo nivel"
}

###
@roleId = {{createRole.response.body.$.id}}

### Consultar role por Id
GET {{baseUrl}}/roles/{{roleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Listar roles (paginado, filtro opcional por trecho do nome)
GET {{baseUrl}}/roles?page=1&pageSize=20&name=suporte
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Atualizar role (descricao ausente/em branco remove a atual)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/roles/{{roleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Suporte N2",
  "description": "Atendimento de segundo nivel e escalonamento"
}

### Vincular permissao a role (idempotente)
POST {{baseUrl}}/roles/{{roleId}}/permissions/{{permissionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Listar permissoes da role
GET {{baseUrl}}/roles/{{roleId}}/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Substituir todas as permissoes da role (tudo ou nada; [] remove todas)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/roles/{{roleId}}/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "permissionIds": ["{{permissionId}}"]
}

### Atribuir role ao usuario (idempotente; vale nas claims a partir do proximo login)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/roles/{{roleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Listar roles do usuario
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Substituir todas as roles do usuario (tudo ou nada; [] remove todas)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roleIds": ["{{roleId}}"]
}

### Novo login - o token passa a trazer as claims "role" e "permission"
# Usa a senha definida em "Trocar senha" acima.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "NovaSenha456"
}

### Remover role do usuario (necessario antes de excluir a role: 409 enquanto atribuida)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/roles/{{roleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Desvincular permissao da role
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/roles/{{roleId}}/permissions/{{permissionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Excluir role (soft delete; o nome pode ser reutilizado)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/roles/{{roleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Excluir permissao (soft delete; 409 se vinculada a role ativa; o mesmo par pode ser recriado depois)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/permissions/{{permissionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Excluir usuario (soft delete)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Liveness
GET {{baseUrl}}/heartbeat

### Health check (dependencias)
GET {{baseUrl}}/healthcheck

### Documento OpenAPI
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi/v1.json
